Language.String:
Real Glass & Water: the glass each building asset has of its own, on every copy of it, in every city. Nothing of it is kept in your saves.

 One Asset element per asset, holding only what it does not take from RealGlass.xml, under the same names and in the same units:
 - a percentage the way its slider shows it: 47 means 47%; GlassThreshold goes from 10 to 95 (lower than in RealGlass.xml: it is this asset's alone);
 - GlassColor as #RRGGBB; GlassNightWindows, InteriorsEnabled and LodGlassFromModel as true or false (LodGlassFromModel: its LOD shows the model's glass, or keeps its own);
 - GlassPreset as the number of a kind of glass (0 Custom, 1 to 10, as in RealGlass.xml); a kind of glass alone gives its color, reflectivity and clarity.

 The building window writes this file (press the building picker's key and click a building). You can edit it while the game is running too: the mod reads it again within a second. Take an asset's element out, or delete the file with the game closed, and it has the global glass again.

Real Glass & Water (Steam Workshop 3823419476): the glass of the building assets in this folder, as their creator set it, for every player who has the mod. A player's own settings for an asset (Alt+G) come first.

 One Asset element per asset, named by the asset's own name (as typed when saving it), holding only what its creator set: everything else follows each player's settings. The same names and units as RealGlassAssets.xml:
 - a percentage the way its slider shows it: 47 means 47%; GlassThreshold goes from 10 to 95;
 - GlassColor as #RRGGBB; GlassNightWindows, InteriorsEnabled and LodGlassFromModel as true or false;
 - GlassPreset as the number of a kind of glass (0 Custom, 1 to 10).

 The asset editor writes this file when the asset is saved (set its glass in the creator window: the mod's key or button there), and puts it into the upload when the asset is shared from the Content Manager. Uploading another way, put this file beside the .crp.
